experiments/
# ...but the bake-off is documentation and belongs in the repository. The bare
# pattern above is inherited and matches a directory of that name at any depth,
# which silently swallowed docs/experiments/ — `git add -A` skipped it without
# a word and several commits looked clean while carrying none of it.
!docs/experiments/
!docs/experiments/**
.cursor/
target/

frontend/src-tauri/binaries/
# Task reports written by agents at the end of a work batch. Working notes for
# the next session, not part of the codebase — and easy to sweep in by accident
# with `git add -A`, which is how two of them already reached a commit.
RAPORT-*.md

# Screenshots taken while testing the app. They are working material for one
# session — the ones the README and the site actually use are committed under
# docs/assets/ and www/, deliberately and by name.
screenshots/
